Checking the ledger: TELL [outcome] requires a strong hit told as it fell, with no better and no worse outcome. The narration says the last volley goes in clean and the drive dies, and the Ashen Wake "drifts down the docking ring, trailing white fire, no longer fighting." That matches a strong hit with the enemy disabled; nothing is narrated as better or worse than that. The BREACH [unsaid] line concerns the player's character speaking, asking, promising or confessing. The narration describes the player's character only in action (swinging guns, holding the scope) and includes no speech or confession. The NOT SO [sheet] line requires that nothing on a sheet changes beyond what TELL names; the narration does not describe any sheet changes. The places, identities, retractions and standing facts sections are all empty, so there is nothing to contradict there.

{
