}

The narration describes a wound: "Bandage first," "unspool the gauze," "The wound has stiffened since the last pass." The ledger's NOT SO line states Mira Kestrel has no wound (health 5 of 5, nothing marked), and the line says the narration must never present the premise as real: no cut, gash, blood, or dressing. The narration treats a wound as real and has her bandaging it, which breaks that line.

Two other points are not contradictions. The dockhand and pilot are not in the recorded identities, so no pronoun conflict can be checked. The narration also does not name the place, so no place conflict exists.

