Checking the narration against obligation line 1 (NOT YET [cost]): the cost is the player's choice, so the narration must not say what it takes. The narration says "The docking costs you: a gash opens on your hand as the clamps take her, and the blood runs down your wrist." That states the cost as already realised: harm taken (a gash, blood). Under line 1, showing the trouble and stopping before saying what it takes is required, and naming the harm breaks that. The other sections (place, identities, binds, retractions, standing) are empty, so nothing else applies.

